  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Write a C program that converts a temperature in Celsius to Fahrenheit. The Celsius temperature should be stored in a float variable celsius, and the Fahrenheit equivalent should be printed using a single printf statement.\nThe relation between the two scales is given as\n\n`fahrenheit = (celsius * 9/5) + 32;\n`Take the celsius temperature to be 20.5.",
    "constraints": [
      "celsius = 20.5"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "No input required.",
    "outputFormat": "Print the Fahrenheit temperature as a floating‑point number with six digits after the decimal point, followed by a newline.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
