    "approach": "The problem asks for a direct conversion from a fixed Celsius value (20.5) to Fahrenheit using the formula fahrenheit = (celsius * 9/5) + 32. Since the input is constant, we simply compute the expression once and print the result with six decimal places. No loops, conditionals, or data structures are needed.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1) – a single arithmetic computation.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) – only a few primitive variables are used.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
